This repository contains two kinds of material under two different licenses.

======================================================================
PART A - BOOK CONTENT: ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
======================================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Selim Medical Press. All rights reserved.

"Signal Management in Medical Device Vigilance" by Dr. Hafez Selim, MD, PhD.
Selim Medical Press, Medical Device Safety Series, Book 5.

Part A covers the book's text, the case dossiers and fictional case data
(including Suturex, Glucalyn, Tessora, Kestran, Orvana, Calvenox, Lumora,
Neoflo and Brevant), figures, tables, explanatory and instructional text,
and the toolkit files T-1 to T-24 and their zip archive in toolkit/.

No part of this material may be reproduced, distributed, or transmitted in
any form or by any means without the prior written permission of the
publisher. Purchasers of the book may download the toolkit files and adapt
them for internal use within their own organization. They may not
redistribute or resell the files, in original or modified form.

The material is provided for education. It is not legal or regulatory
advice. Thresholds, scores, bands, matrices and timelines are illustrative
examples, not regulatory requirements.

======================================================================
PART B - WEB TOOL SOURCE CODE: MIT LICENSE
======================================================================

Part B covers the HTML, CSS and JavaScript source code of tool/index.html
and index.html (the software). It does not cover the book content from
Part A that appears in those files as text, such as the module
descriptions, scoring anchors and book example data.

